flowchart TB
    accTitle: Selection can choose or reject the candidate set
    accDescr: Candidate actions and their values enter selection. Selection may carry one action forward to execution or reject the proposed set and return to proposal. Rejection is a selection outcome, not an evaluation result or an executed action.

    PAIRS[Candidate actions and values]
    SELECT[Selection]
    CHOOSE[Select one action]
    EXEC[Execution]
    REJECT[Reject current proposals]
    PROP[Return to proposal]
    PAIRS --> SELECT
    SELECT --> CHOOSE --> EXEC
    SELECT --> REJECT --> PROP

    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef result fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px;
    classDef alternative fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    class SELECT process;
    class CHOOSE,EXEC result;
    class PAIRS,REJECT,PROP alternative;
